# GitHub pull requests

The GitHub App token in this Cloud Agent sandbox cannot create pull requests.
`gh pr create` returns `403 Resource not accessible by integration`. Git push works.

Never tell the user to "check your branches" for that error. The branch is usually already on GitHub.

Required workflow:

1. Commit and `git push -u origin <branch>`.
2. Create or update the PR with the **ManagePullRequest** tool. Do not use `gh pr create`.
3. On push to `cursor/**`, `.github/workflows/open-cursor-pr.yml` also opens a PR if none exists.

If ManagePullRequest fails, point the user at
`https://github.com/TimothyHolmsten/change_flare/compare/main...<branch>?expand=1`.
